[
    {
        "content": "<p>I am currently having AI agents write and verify RISC-V assembly code using a separation logic in Lean. The process turned out to be agent-friendly. I wrote a blog post about it <a href=\"https://blog.zksecurity.xyz/posts/end-coding/\">https://blog.zksecurity.xyz/posts/end-coding/</a></p>",
        "id": 591831641,
        "sender_full_name": "Yoichi Hirai",
        "timestamp": 1777477053
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I do think this model of using a proof assistant to reason about assembly is very cool, and probably the right way to approach certain tasks. I think sel4 does something similar with Isabelle reasoning about bytecode from an untrusted compiler.</p>\n<p>I will say that this is maybe not the best example of a spec if one of the suggestions is that we can potentially dispense with higher level languages. This is probably partly my lack of familiarity with the domain and maybe some custom notation, but it's a little obtuse.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">cpsTriple</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">base</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">base</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">120</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">code</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"c1\">-- Registers + memory</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x12</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sp</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x7</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v7</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v6</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v5</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x11</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v11</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"n\">evmWordIs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">evmWordIs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">32</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"c1\">-- Registers + memory (updated)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x12</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">32</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x7</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">result3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">carry3b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">carry3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">x11</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↦ᵣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">carry3a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span>\n<span class=\"w\">       </span><span class=\"n\">evmWordIs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">sp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">**</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">evmWordIs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">32</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 591998670,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Bailey",
        "timestamp": 1777540317
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The topmost specification will be a simpler connection to <a href=\"https://github.com/NethermindEth/EVMYulLean\">EVMYulLean</a>. Below that topmost level, there will be lots of lemmas mentioning concrete registers because that's needed for the next (previous) assembly code snippets.</p>",
        "id": 592006113,
        "sender_full_name": "Yoichi Hirai",
        "timestamp": 1777542215
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"228466\">Chris Bailey</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/236449-Program-verification/topic/RISC-V.20separation.20logic.20in.20Lean/near/591998670\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I will say that this is maybe not the best example of a spec if one of the suggestions is that we can potentially dispense with higher level languages. This is probably partly my lack of familiarity with the domain and maybe some custom notation, but it's a little obtuse.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Or perhaps not enough custom notation.? The name <code>triple</code> evokes notation with arguments 1&amp;4, 3, and 2&amp;5 more tightly grouped. But up to permutation that's how dense a sequent would need to look if it had to talk about memory addresses</p>",
        "id": 592117994,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris C",
        "timestamp": 1777570190
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>with arguments 1&amp;4, 3, and 2&amp;5 more tightly grouped</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You're reading it right. The current layout puts very short arguments in front so that it's easier to see.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>custom notation</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>That's a right instinct. <code>evmWordIs sp a</code> is defined as a separating conjunction of four things (each is again a conjunction).</p>",
        "id": 592129963,
        "sender_full_name": "Yoichi Hirai",
        "timestamp": 1777573465
    }
]